@title Password and MFA FAQ
@subtitle The new staff password and multi-factor authentication policy
@author IT team, Cinder Valley School District

A new password and multi-factor authentication (MFA) policy for all staff accounts takes effect on November 3, 2026. This page answers the most common questions about what is changing and how to get help.

!! IT will never ask for your password or your code by email or phone. If someone does, it is a scam: do not reply, and report it to the help desk.

# Why are we changing the policy?
Two phishing incidents in 2026 compromised staff mailboxes. Longer passwords and a second factor make a stolen password far less useful to an attacker.

# What changes on November 3?
- Passwords must be at least 14 characters.
- Every staff account needs multi-factor authentication.

# Do I have to change my password every 90 days?
No. We are removing forced rotation. We will only ask you to change your password after a suspected compromise.

# What if I do not have a smartphone?
The help desk will issue you a hardware key at no cost.

# What if I lose my phone or key?
Call the help desk at extension 4400. They will give you a temporary bypass code that is valid for 24 hours while you set up a replacement.

# Who do I contact for help?
The help desk, at extension 4400. It is open 07:00 to 17:00 on school days.
